BT /F2 17.0 Tf 93.20 699.00 Td (Sparse Curriculum Sampling for Efficient Fine-Tuning) Tj ET
BT /F2 17.0 Tf 199.33 678.00 Td (of Small Language Models) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 245.89 656.50 Td (An Tran and Laura Hayes) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 194.54 643.00 Td (Demo Institute of Computing \(fictional affiliation\)) Tj ET
BT /F2 11.5 Tf 283.64 615.00 Td (Abstract) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.0 Tf 97.00 600.20 Td (Fine-tuning a pretrained language model on a new task usually requires many passes over the) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.0 Tf 97.00 587.40 Td (training set, even though a large fraction of the examples are already handled well after the) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.0 Tf 97.00 574.60 Td (first epoch. We propose Sparse Curriculum Sampling \(SCS\), a simple data selection method) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.0 Tf 97.00 561.80 Td (that estimates the difficulty of each example from its recent loss and samples hard examples) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.0 Tf 97.00 549.00 Td (more often while still revisiting easy ones. SCS adds no trainable parameters and can be) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.0 Tf 97.00 536.20 Td (implemented in a few lines of code. On three text classification benchmarks, SCS reaches the) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.0 Tf 97.00 523.40 Td (accuracy of standard fine-tuning while using 38% fewer gradient updates, and it reduces the) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.0 Tf 97.00 510.60 Td (variance across random seeds. We also discuss when the method fails and why its gains may) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.0 Tf 97.00 497.80 Td (not transfer to generation tasks.) Tj ET
BT /F2 12.0 Tf 72.00 464.80 Td (1 Introduction) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 72.00 448.20 Td (Small language models with fewer than one billion parameters remain attractive for laboratories and) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 72.00 434.60 Td (companies with limited computing budgets. However, fine-tuning such a model still involves a) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 72.00 421.00 Td (trade-off between cost and accuracy: training for more epochs tends to improve the final score, but) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 72.00 407.40 Td (most of the additional computation is spent on examples that the model has already learned.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 72.00 386.80 Td (Curriculum learning [2] addresses a related problem by presenting examples in a meaningful order,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 72.00 373.20 Td (usually from easy to hard. In practice, a fixed curriculum requires a difficulty measure defined before) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 72.00 359.60 Td (training, which is often unavailable for new datasets. In this paper, we take a different view: instead) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 72.00 346.00 Td (of ordering the data once, we let the model's own training signal decide how often each example) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 72.00 332.40 Td (should be seen.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 72.00 311.80 Td (Our contributions are threefold. First, we introduce SCS, a sampling rule based on an exponential) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 72.00 298.20 Td (moving average of the per-example loss. Second, we show empirically that SCS reduces the) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 72.00 284.60 Td (number of gradient updates without hurting accuracy. Third, we analyze the failure cases of the) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 72.00 271.00 Td (method, which, to the best of our knowledge, have not been reported for similar approaches.) Tj ET
BT /F2 12.0 Tf 72.00 241.00 Td (2 Method) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 72.00 224.40 Td (Let D = {\(x_i, y_i\)}, i = 1..N, be the training set and f\(x; w\) a classifier with weights w. At step t, we) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 72.00 210.80 Td (keep a difficulty score s_i for every example, updated whenever the example is visited:) Tj ET
BT /F4 10.0 Tf 156.00 185.80 Td (s_i <- beta * s_i + \(1 - beta\) * L\(f\(x_i; w\), y_i\)) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 527.17 185.80 Td (\(1\)) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 72.00 160.20 Td (where L is the cross-entropy loss and beta is a smoothing factor set to 0.9 in all experiments.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 72.00 146.60 Td (Examples are then drawn with probability) Tj ET
BT /F4 10.0 Tf 159.00 121.60 Td (p_i = \(s_i + eps\)^alpha / sum_j \(s_j + eps\)^alpha) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 527.17 121.60 Td (\(2\)) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 72.00 96.00 Td (The exponent alpha controls how strongly the sampler focuses on hard examples: alpha = 0) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 72.00 82.40 Td (recovers uniform sampling, whereas large values concentrate the probability mass on a small) Tj ET
72.00 70.00 m 222.00 70.00 l 0.4 w S
BT /F3 8 Tf 72.00 60.00 Td (* This is a fictional paper written for the PaperViet demo. The method and all numbers are invented; only the references are real.) Tj ET
